<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="aitext">
    <exampledescription>Identify the hazard in an image of a blocked fire exit. The AI prompt describes the image in text because the grader cannot see it.</exampledescription>
    <name>
      <text>Workplace hazard identification: fire exit</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><img src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/blocked_fire_exit.svg" alt="Warehouse corridor with an emergency fire exit door blocked by stacked cardboard boxes and a pallet" width="640" height="420"></p>
<p>Inspect the workplace scenario shown in the image. Identify the primary OSHA/safety hazard present and state the risk it poses.</p>]]></text>
      <file name="blocked_fire_exit.svg" path="/" encoding="base64"></file>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The emergency fire exit is obstructed by boxes stacked on a pallet. Exit routes must be kept clear at all times (OSHA 29 CFR 1910.37). In a fire or other emergency, workers could be delayed or trapped, leading to injury or death.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>10</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>hs-fire-exit-hazard</idnumber>
    <responseformat>plain</responseformat>
    <responsefieldlines>5</responsefieldlines>
    <minwordlimit/>
    <maxwordlimit>150</maxwordlimit>
    <graderinfo format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Expected answer: blocked/obstructed fire exit (egress obstruction); risk of delayed or prevented evacuation in a fire or emergency.</p>]]></text>
    </graderinfo>
    <responsetemplate format="html">
      <text/>
    </responsetemplate>
    <aiprompt>You cannot see the image the student was shown, so use this description of it: a warehouse corridor with a red emergency door marked "FIRE EXIT - KEEP CLEAR" under a green EXIT sign. Cardboard boxes are stacked on a wooden pallet directly in front of the door, blocking it. Shelving is on the left and a wall-mounted fire extinguisher on the right; neither is a hazard. Determine if the student accurately pinpoints the safety hazard shown (the blocked fire exit / obstructed emergency egress) and mentions the risk of restricted or delayed evacuation in an emergency.</aiprompt>
    <markscheme>10 marks for identifying the specific hazard (blocked or obstructed fire exit) and the safety risk (people cannot evacuate quickly or could be trapped in a fire or emergency). 5 marks if they mention a hazard is present but are vague, for example "boxes are in the way" or "fire hazard" without saying the exit is blocked or what the risk is. 0 marks for incorrect identification, such as naming the shelving or fire extinguisher as the hazard.</markscheme>
    <model/>
    <spellcheck>0</spellcheck>
    <sampleresponse>
      <response>The fire exit door is blocked by boxes stacked on a pallet. In a fire, workers would not be able to get out quickly and could be trapped.</response>
    </sampleresponse>
    <sampleresponse>
      <response>There are boxes left lying around, which is a hazard.</response>
    </sampleresponse>
    <sampleresponse>
      <response>The fire extinguisher is mounted too low on the wall.</response>
    </sampleresponse>
    <tags>
      <tag><text>subject:health-safety</text></tag>
      <tag><text>topic:hazard-identification</text></tag>
      <tag><text>level:professional</text></tag>
      <tag><text>feature:samples</text></tag>
      <tag><text>feature:image</text></tag>
    </tags>
  </question>
</quiz>
